            <ArticleTitle>Painful knee--an unusual cause secondary to pseudomonas septic arthritis of the hip.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>152</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A child presented with knee pain, the cause of pain was found on further investigation to be due chondrolysis of the hip joint secondary to a pseudomonas aeruginosa septic arthritis. The patient functionally did well following a subtotal synovectomy and prolonged treatment with appropriate antibiotics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
